@page "/SteamElectrical"
@implements IDisposable

<PageTitle>Steam-Electric Concept | Clean Energy Design</PageTitle>

<div class="se-page">

    <!-- NAV -->
    <nav class="se-nav">
        <span class="se-nav-brand">⚙ STEAM-ELECTRIC</span>

        <ul class="se-nav-links">
            <li><a href="#concept">Concept</a></li>
            <li><a href="#schematic">Schematic</a></li>
            <li><a href="#calculator">Calculator</a></li>
            <li><a href="#truck">Truck</a></li>
            <li><a href="#impact">Impact</a></li>
            <li><a href="#safety">Safety</a></li>
        </ul>
    </nav>

    <!-- HERO -->
    <section class="se-hero">
        <div class="se-hero-grid"></div>

        <span class="se-badge">CONCEPT DESIGN · OPEN SOURCE IDEA</span>

        <h1>
            The <span>Steam-Electric</span><br />
            Vehicle System
        </h1>

        <p>
            A closed-loop steam propulsion concept using battery-powered heating,
            PWM control, and multi-axle electric motors.
            Built around existing technology and thermodynamic principles.
        </p>

        <div class="se-hero-stats">
            <div class="se-stat">
                <div class="n">3×</div>
                <div class="l">Concept torque advantage</div>
            </div>

            <div class="se-stat">
                <div class="n">0</div>
                <div class="l">Combustion events</div>
            </div>

            <div class="se-stat">
                <div class="n">~40</div>
                <div class="l">Illustrative moving parts</div>
            </div>

            <div class="se-stat">
                <div class="n">H₂O</div>
                <div class="l">Working fluid</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CONCEPT -->
    <div id="concept">
        <section class="se-section">

            <div class="se-section-sub">The Idea</div>

            <h2 class="se-section-title">
                Three component swaps. One electrical overhaul.
            </h2>

            <p class="se-section-lead">
                This concept explores replacing the conventional combustion powertrain
                with a steam-based mechanical system and electrical architecture.
                The chassis, suspension, brakes, and body could remain conceptually
                separate from the propulsion system.
            </p>

            <div class="se-card-grid">

                <div class="se-card">
                    <div class="se-card-icon">🔁</div>
                    <h3>Engine → Steam Cylinders</h3>
                    <p>
                        A steam piston engine can provide mechanical torque through
                        a crankshaft. A double-acting multi-cylinder configuration
                        is shown here as a conceptual architecture.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="se-card">
                    <div class="se-card-icon">💧</div>
                    <h3>Fuel Tank → Water Tank</h3>
                    <p>
                        Water acts as the working fluid. A condenser can recover
                        exhaust steam and return condensed water to the system.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="se-card">
                    <div class="se-card-icon">⚡</div>
                    <h3>Generator Loop</h3>
                    <p>
                        The steam engine can mechanically drive a generator while
                        electric motors provide propulsion in an electric-drive
                        architecture.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="se-card">
                    <div class="se-card-icon">🎛</div>
                    <h3>PWM Controller = Heat Control</h3>
                    <p>
                        A power controller can regulate electrical heating input.
                        Actual thermal efficiency depends on the heater, boiler,
                        insulation, operating pressure, and cycle design.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="se-card">
                    <div class="se-card-icon">🔄</div>
                    <h3>Closed Loop by Design</h3>
                    <p>
                        Water can be evaporated, expanded, condensed, and returned
                        to the feed system. Some makeup water may still be required.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="se-card">
                    <div class="se-card-icon">🏭</div>
                    <h3>Manufacturing Concept</h3>
                    <p>
                        The design attempts to reduce some conventional combustion
                        components, while recognizing that boilers, pumps, condensers,
                        controls, and pressure hardware introduce their own complexity.
                    </p>
                </div>

            </div>
        </section>
    </div>

